<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n800" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγοστός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>flat of the hand</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i>, in the phrase 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ δ᾽ ἐν κονίῃσι πεσὼν ἕλε γαῖαν
					ἀγοστῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.425
				</span></i>
			, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρὸς ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.120
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>arm</i>, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκάλη</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				17.129
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.464
			</span></i> (Antip.); pl., ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.254.15
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.): metaph., [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀκαδημείας] ἐν ἀγοστῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					150
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>dirt, filth</i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.506
			</span></i>. (Perh. cognate with Skt. <i>haástas</i>
			'hand'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
